WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.010
Ukraine is the Paris Hilton of countries…
anytime it’s in the news, it’s not for

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.010
anything good.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.570
For the last few decades, Ukraine has been
the

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:20.230
scene of the worst nuclear catastrophe, a
military conflict with Russia and the biggest

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.560
corruption scandals you can imagine.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:33.470
But… look, there is another thing Ukrainian
politicians have in common with Paris Hilton:

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.360
they both have a lot of money.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.380
After the fall of the

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.370
Soviet Union, Ukraine’s economy stopped
being managed by the state and started being

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.540
managed by the state’s friends.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.540
These are the so called

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.790
oligarchs and you can find them in all of
the country’s political parties, pro Russian

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.489
and anti Russian alike.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:51.809
For example, the current

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:55.920
president, PETRO POROSHENKO is also known
as the ‘King of Chocolate’ because he

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:02.420
owns the biggest chocolate company in the
country.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.420
And the

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.340
former president, YULIA TIMISHENKO is known
as the ‘Gas Princess’ because she made

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.030
a lot of money in the gas industry.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.710
In other words: things

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.270
changed, but everything stayed the same.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.610
Nonetheless, things are really starting to
change in Ukraine.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.880
But, make no mistake; these changes are not
for the better.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.340
In fact, the opposite

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.340
is true.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.180
You see, in a previous video, we told you
how Russia is Europe’s main gas provider.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.470
For example, Germany buys 60% of their natural
gas from

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.350
Russian companies like GAZPROM or ROSNEFT.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.220
And how does this gas arrive?

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.220
Well…

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.020
most of it comes from gas pipes that cross
Ukrainian soil.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.330
So what does this all mean?

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:44.549
It means that, despite Ukraine having little
gas resources, they are still a hot spot in

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:45.619
this business.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:47.060
And this… is

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.400
when Vladimir Putin comes into the picture!

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:57.689
To this day, Putin needs Ukraine to supply
Europe with gas.

00:01:57.689 --> 00:02:02.420
But, as you know, the relationship between
Putin and Kiev currently has a status of

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:08.530
‘it’s complicated’, to say the least.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:13.300
So after decades of love and Slavic fraternity,
the Government of Ukrainian president Poroshenko

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.300
wants to

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.840
stay away from Putin as much as possible.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.600
As you can imagine, this political divorce
doesn’t make Russia happy.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.870
Anytime their gas goes through Ukrainian territory,
they have to pay a

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.740
millionaire’s share of alimony to their
ex wife.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.459
But this is not the end of the story!

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:33.480
As long as Ukraine is in the center of the
gas routes,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.880
Kiev will have a better position to negotiate
with Moscow and even Brussels.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:43.250
In other words: Ukraine matters as long as
we need them for gas.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.760
So what’s Putin’s strategy, then?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.680
Well, check this out.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:55.010
Russians Insist On New Pipeline To Bypass
Ukraine, And Europeans Fine With It

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.190
Yes, my dear viewers, Russia wants to take
Ukraine out of the gas route equation.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.720
This way, Ukraine would lose their strategic
value, which

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:08.030
would mean that neither America, nor the European
Union would really care about them in the

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.840
case of a potential new Russian invasion.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.300
So the question now is…

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.400
Can this strategy work?

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.030
Will the European Union let Russia bypass
Ukraine?

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.640
Today we’re going to answer all of these

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:24.370
questions but, before we do, let’s take
a look back at the history.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:31.150
IF YOU ARE NOT MINE, THEN YOU WILL NOT BE
ANYBODY ELSE’S

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.800
In the year 2000, 70% of the Russian gas arriving
to Europe came from Ukraine.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.090
More specifically, it came from the so called
BROTHERHOOD gas

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.090
pipe.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.930
This pipeline was built in the times of the
Soviet Union and it become more important

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.640
as the demand for Russian gas grew.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.640
The other 30%

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.030
came from the YAMAL pipe, in Belarus, but
that’s another story.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.819
When the Soviet Union fell apart, Ukraine
became an independent nation.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:02.170
And this was the moment when the Kiev politicians
started to see the

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:05.420
business clearly.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:13.439
“Russia has the gas reserves but they need
us to sell to the Germans so… they should

00:04:13.439 --> 00:04:14.900
pay us a fare.”

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.799
Nowadays, this fare is more than 2 billion
dollars a year, but it used to be even higher.

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:21.239
Thanks to the so called TRANSIT RIGHTS, the
State

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:28.000
owned gas company in Ukraine, NAFTOGAZ, became
a behemoth: all of this, despite having almost

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.900
no gas resources in the country.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.781
As you can imagine, this isn’t just about
economics here.

00:04:32.781 --> 00:04:35.990
Both in Russia and Ukraine, everything is
a political weapon.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:36.990
So anytime Kiev had a

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.780
Russian friendly government, GAZPROM sold
them cheap gas.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:45.260
But when Kiev didn’t have Russian friendly
politicians in office, prices went sky

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.850
high.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:54.150
We already discussed this in another video,
the first one in this series on Russian Gas.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:57.410
The gas negotiations between Russia and Ukraine
led to

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.390
a supply cut in 2006 and 2009.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:05.870
The last one, in 2009, caused the rest of
Europe to go without gas too.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:09.810
And this was when Russia started a new strategy.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:16.120
Putin phoned his friend, the former German
chancellor and current ROSNEFT president,

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.120
GERHARD

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.120
SCHROEDER.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:25.900
And GERHARD SCHROEDER phoned the current German
chancellor, ANGELA MERKEL.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.390
This is how they sold the first project to
bypass Ukraine:

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.520
the NORD STREAM 1 pipeline.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.310
This pipeline goes through the Baltic sea,
straight from Russia to Germany.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.640
One year later, in 2010, YANUKOVICH won the
Ukrainian presidency.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.080
YANUKOVICH is a Pro Russian politician.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.910
So the good times and the cheap gas

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.120
prices came back.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.930
But in 2014, we had the EUROMAIDAN.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.420
Do you remember those protests in Kiev?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.380
This took YANUKOVICH out of office and brought
a

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.389
brand new anti Russian government to Ukraine.

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:04.319
And this is when Putin said
“If I can’t have you, nobody can.”

00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:10.770
Since 2015, GAZPROM, Russia’s main gas company,
started the ultimate plan to bypass Ukraine.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.900
For one, they started the NORDSTREAM 2, through
the

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.070
Baltic.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:22.830
And on the Southern side, Gazprom is building
the TURKSTREAM, that sends gas through the

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.360
BLACK SEA as far as Turkey.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.360
According to the

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:30.009
GAZPROM president, by the year 2020, that
good old Brotherhood pipeline will carry less

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:32.590
than 10% of what it used to.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:33.650
But hold on just a second!

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:40.100
Because, so far, it seems like Russia is just
plain bad and Ukraine is a poor victim, right?

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.199
In fact, things are far

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:43.199
more complicated.

00:06:43.199 --> 00:06:50.880
Let’s dig deeper into this, shall we?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.360
THE UKRAINIAN JUGGERNAUT
Naftogaz is far more than a gas company.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.310
In fact, it’s sort of a job agency!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.289
They have more than 175,000 workers.

00:06:59.289 --> 00:07:00.960
Yes, you heard that right.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:01.960
To

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.840
put that into perspective, the equivalent
of Naftogaz in Poland, PGNIG, which is also

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.169
owned by the state, only employs 25,000 people.

00:07:09.169 --> 00:07:14.479
In other words, in Ukraine, you’re nobody
if you don’t have a relative working for

00:07:14.479 --> 00:07:15.479
Naftogaz.

00:07:15.479 --> 00:07:19.500
As you can imagine, Naftogaz is a black hole
on Ukrainians’ finances.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.169
It’s like if Paris Hilton was taking care
of the accounting.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:23.169
You know,

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:27.660
with so many people working for a state owned
enterprise, money disappears and nobody knows

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.160
why.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.050
According to the Institute for Economic

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:39.440
Research and Policy Consulting, a Ukrainian
think tank, NAFTOGAZ loses more than 3 billion

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.170
dollars a year from corruption.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.170
This company is

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.210
always reporting financial loses.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:46.310
And we aren’t talking about a little bit
of money here.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:50.361
Just in 2014, Naftogaz losses accounted for
6% of the

00:07:50.361 --> 00:07:52.300
entire Ukrainian GDP.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.900
But right there, in 2014, we had the Euromaidan.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.470
And that meant very fast changes.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:04.030
Changes like this one.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:08.220
Ukrainian police detain Naftogaz Chairman
of Board Yevhen Bakulin

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.800
The new CEO of the company is this man you
see on the screen, ANDRIY KOBOLIEV, a 40 year

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.910
old consultant.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.370
His job could be summarized in two

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.050
goals: ending corruption and ending Russian
dependency.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:21.919
And now you might wonder… is he serious
about this?

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:24.100
Well… so far, things look good.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.110
Both the European Union and IMF have pushed
Ukraine to do

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:32.099
their homework and, it seems like they are
trying…

00:08:32.099 --> 00:08:40.310
GSE announces new improvements of the storage
transparency initiative - Naftogaz of Ukraine

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:46.990
joins Gas Storage Inventory (AGSI+)
Since then, Naftogaz has started to make a

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:47.990
profit.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.490
After decades of financial losses, now they
account for 13% to the Ukrainian state’s

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.490
income.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.920
And now you might wonder… what did KOBOLYEV
do?

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.060
What was his magic formula?

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:59.130
First of all, as is always the case with state
monopolies, the prices were controlled by

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.170
the Government.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.269
This meant really cheap gas, and

00:09:02.269 --> 00:09:06.070
Ukrainian consumers who were used to paying
these artificially low prices.

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:09.310
Now, Naftogaz has raised prices to a level
equal to that of other

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.830
European countries.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:16.519
Second of all, Kobolyev has confronted Putin
with a lot of… lateral thinking.

00:09:16.519 --> 00:09:20.240
You see, Gazprom wanted to raise gas prices
for Ukraine.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.240
But not

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.680
for the rest of the European countries.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.380
So what did Ukraine do?

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.050
Instead of fighting with Moskow, they started
to buy gas from other European

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.050
countries like…

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.050
Slovakia.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.990
But, wait, wait a minute here…

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:34.530
Does Slovakia have gas resources?

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.920
Of course not!

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:40.470
Listen to this.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:46.970
The contracts with GAZPROM say that, once
the gas arrives in an EU country, Russia loses

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:47.970
control over it.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:48.970
This means that, the buyer can do

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:55.900
whatever they want with the gas.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:01.940
So now, Slovakia gets their Russian gas through
the Brotherhood pipe and, then, it goes through

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:02.940
the same pipe,

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:04.140
back to Ukraine.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:08.380
So Slovakia buys Russian gas and then Ukraine
buys it from Slovakia.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.779
Thanks to this, Naftogaz has cut a fourth
of their

00:10:10.779 --> 00:10:12.640
importing costs.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.260
But this is just the beginning!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.620
Kobolyev keeps looking for alternatives!

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.770
For example?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:18.850
AZERBAIJAN.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.649
As we said in other videos, Azerbaijan has

00:10:20.649 --> 00:10:21.829
lots of gas.

00:10:21.829 --> 00:10:26.900
And they are building a pipeline, the TRANS
ANATOLIAN, which goes to Italy.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.210
Kiev wants to connect to this pipe through
Bulgaria.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:34.400
But… we’ll dig deeper into this in our
closing video for this series.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.860
Because, believe me, Azerbaijan is another
interesting topic that deserves

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.860
a video on its own.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.209
If you don’t want to miss it, don’t forget
to subscribe.

00:10:42.209 --> 00:10:47.350
So going back to our story, it seems that
Ukraine is doing a great job cleaning up corruption,

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.350
right?

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.380
Well… wait a minute because, as we always

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:54.140
say on VisualPolitik, not everything is all
sunshine and rainbows.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:58.170
If Ukraine wants to fully adapt to European
standards, they should liberalize

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.170
their gas market.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:03.029
This would mean that Naftogaz would no longer
be a monopoly and they would have to split

00:11:03.029 --> 00:11:05.260
the company into several, smaller

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.260
ones.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:11.070
One would be focused on gas production, another
one would manage domestic consumption… and

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.070
so on.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:15.350
And, as you can imagine, this is where

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:19.899
the problems come in!

00:11:19.899 --> 00:11:25.579
EU and Ukraine in tug of war over Naftogaz
unbundling

00:11:25.579 --> 00:11:29.780
As you can imagine, as much as Kobolyev wants
to clean up the company, too many oligarchs

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:32.320
have been too good to the company for too
long.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.320
Yes,

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.890
the company can be owned by the state but…
this is no excuse to not have millionaire

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.740
salaries and millionaire bribes.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.161
And this is hard to just

00:11:41.161 --> 00:11:42.161
stop from one day to the next.

00:11:42.161 --> 00:11:43.529
But this is not the worst part!

00:11:43.529 --> 00:11:46.570
You see… in march 2019, Ukraine will have
elections again.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:49.670
And the result will be decisive for Naftogaz’s

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:50.670
future.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:54.300
And… of course, my dear viewers, Russia
has a perfectly defined agenda for this.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:12:02.940
Let’s have a look at it!

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:07.880
ECONOMICS VERSUS GEOPOLITICS
Germany has made it all clear: they will build

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.700
the NORDSTREAM 2 pipeline.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.330
Both Brussels and Washington are against it.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.450
In fact, Donald Trump has

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:17.640
been the biggest critic.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:21.389
He kind of said that even Paris Hilton would
do a better job than Germany when it comes

00:12:21.389 --> 00:12:23.040
to having a good energy policy.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.540
And now you might wonder…

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:30.080
How is it possible that Angela Merkel has
let herself be seduced by Vladimir Putin?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.579
Yes, you know that the former

00:12:32.579 --> 00:12:35.890
German chancellor, Gerhard Schroeder, is Putin’s
man in Europe.

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:39.160
But… there is more to it than that.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.640
Basically, Germany has a big dilemma.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:45.430
On one hand, their industry needs gas.

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.149
A LOT of gas.

00:12:47.149 --> 00:12:49.589
The safer and cheaper, the better.

00:12:49.589 --> 00:12:50.790
And, putting

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.880
politics aside, NordStream 2 is the best option
economy wise.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:55.880
First, it is cheap.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.850
Second, it avoids all the potential gas wars
with Ukraine.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.959
The problem?

00:12:58.959 --> 00:13:01.990
This gaspipe would make Germany even more
dependent on Russia.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.380
Meanwhile, Putin is happy.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.870
He can bypass Ukraine and also, destroy their
economy.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:10.120
In this regard, Russia’s intentions are
more obvious than your

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.120
ex girlfriend’s when she wanted to “have
a coffee with you”.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.120
Want an example?

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:17.040
Have a look at this map!

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.040
This is the Black sea.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.779
And this little sea to the North is the AZOV
sea.

00:13:20.779 --> 00:13:23.389
Both seas are connected by the KERCH strait.

00:13:23.389 --> 00:13:24.501
And Ukraine has two

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:27.040
important harbours in the AZOV sea.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.370
So what did Russia do?

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.459
They built a bridge right at the Kerch strait.

00:13:30.459 --> 00:13:32.350
A bridge that makes most of the ships

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:35.300
unable to arrive or to leave the Azov sea.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:39.940
This is why you hear so much news about military
escalation in this region now.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.170
So now you might wonder… why is Russia trying
so hard to bankrupt Ukraine?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.019
It is all about jealousy?

00:13:45.019 --> 00:13:46.940
Of course not!

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:47.940
The thing is… the worse the

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:52.529
anti Russian Ukrainian government does, the
better things are for the pro Russian candidates

00:13:52.529 --> 00:13:54.310
in the elections.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:14:01.949
And is there any pro Russian candidate running
in the 2019 Ukrainian elections?

00:14:01.949 --> 00:14:05.579
Well… the answer is… anything is possible
here!

00:14:05.579 --> 00:14:08.209
Here’s an example of how crazy this country
can be.

00:14:08.209 --> 00:14:11.380
In Ukraine they have a TV show called ‘Servant
of the people’.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.449
The star is a teacher who

00:14:12.449 --> 00:14:13.449
fights corruption.

00:14:13.449 --> 00:14:19.040
OK, so there’s already an actual political
party based on this series.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.420
The actor who plays the role of that teacher
is the

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.420
candidate.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.420
His name is VLADIMIR ZELENSKY.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:27.130
And… does he have any real chance of winning?

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.310
Well… just look at this.

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:37.389
Tymoshenko leading presidential candidate
poll, followed by Poroshenko, Zelensky and

00:14:37.389 --> 00:14:39.070
Hrytsenko
Yes, you heard that right.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:43.490
He’s in the third place, followed by the
King of Chocolate and the Gas Princess.

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.160
So… yes, it is impossible to predict

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.320
what’s going to happen.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:50.940
There is just one clear thing in this story.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:54.250
And that’s that AZERBAIJAN is having a really
good time.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.250
But we’ll talk

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.450
about this in the next video.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.060
So in the meantime, the question for you is…

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.930
What would you do if you were Germany?

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:01.930
Would you take that cheap

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.260
Russian gas in exchange for leaving Ukraine
alone?

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.490
Or you would sacrifice competitiveness for
political interest?

